-- Dire Maul West (map 429): the plan for the run leader (.bot run), exported from turtle-agent 940fc091
-- (dungeons/dire_maul_west.json) with the options of the header of 20261017130000:
--   turtle-agent plan-export --mmaps <map 429 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops --rev 940fc091 \
--     --stamp 20261024153600 --out <dir> dire_maul_west
-- Stacks on 20261024153000. Round 3 of the Dire Maul West fixes, for the crystal event and the Immol'thar leg (r36 slotD,
-- 2026-10-24: stopped at step 465, the Immol'thar boss row, 3x "took more than 300 s out of combat"; the party at -7.1 853.4 -31.1;
-- the three neutral Highborne Summoners 11466 at 100 % stood near it, and steps 421/425 wiped 5 times on the ring's patrols).
--
-- SCRIPT FACTS (tortoise-wow, read 2026-10-24):
--   * Immol'thar's prison is the five CrystalGenerator gameobjects: dire_maul.h:57-61 (GO_CRISTAL_1..5_EVENT = 177259, 177257,
--     177258, 179504, 179505), registered in instance_dire_maul.cpp:113-127. Their spawns: tw_world_gameobject.sql guids 261760
--     (16.7865 277.154 -8.4683), 261762 (111.851 436.077 28.6016), 262113 (-85.1898 444.665 28.6016), 262115
--     (71.097 874.454 -24.5794), 262117 (-130.415 712.951 -24.579). Each is a BUTTON (gameobject_template 177259 etc. type 1,
--     data2 autoCloseTime 0), so DoUseDoorOrButton sets it GO_STATE_ACTIVE and it stays active (ScriptedInstance.cpp:11-31,
--     GameObject.cpp:1384-1400).
--   * The event's mobs are the Mana Remnants 11483 (NPC_RESTE_MANA, dire_maul.h:43) and the Arcane Aberrations 11480
--     (dire_maul.h:44): on the first of either that dies, instance_dire_maul::SetData64(TYPE_CRISTAL_EVENT, guid) calls
--     DoSortCristalsEventMobs (instance_dire_maul.cpp:450-457, 555-581), which puts every ALIVE one within 20.0 yd of a crystal
--     into that crystal's list (571). Every death then removes it from every list (460-471); a crystal whose list becomes empty is
--     used (DoUseDoorOrButton, 467) and forgotten (471). When all five lists are empty, SetData(TYPE_CRISTAL_EVENT, DONE)
--     (479) opens the force field 179503 and the magic vortex 179506 (DoUseDoorOrButton, 264-265), removes Immol'thar's
--     UNIT_FLAG_NOT_SELECTABLE|UNIT_FLAG_SPAWNING (EnableCreature, instance_dire_maul.cpp:10-15, 261-271; the flags are set at
--     212-213 until DONE), and turns the Highborne Summoners 11466 (NPC_IMMOL_THAR_GARDIEN, 11466, dire_maul.h:40) hostile
--     (faction 100) onto him: EnableCreature + SetFactionTemplateId(100) + AttackStart(ImmolThar) for each guardian within 100 yd
--     (276-295). Immol'thar is attackable only after that; boss_immol_thar.cpp has no prison logic (its AI is Trample, Infected
--     Bite, Eye of Immol'thar, Portal of Immol'thar, Enrage).
--   * The twenty Mana Remnants are five groups of four, one group per crystal (tw_world_creature.sql, map 429, entry 11483):
--     177259: 28.1 277.3, 6.1 277.3, 17.1 266.3, 17.1 288.3 (all |dz| <= 4 of -8.5); 177257: 103.7 428.02, 119.3 428.02,
--     119.3 443.58, 103.7 443.58 (z 28.6); 177258: -85.3 456, -96.3 445, -74.3 445, -85.3 434 (z 28.6); 179504: 62.92 882.38,
--     62.92 866.82, 78.48 866.82, 78.48 882.38 (z -24.58); 179505: -137.98 705.02, -122.42 720.58, -137.98 720.58,
--     -122.42 705.02 (z -24.58). npc_template 11483: faction 834 (hostile), level 57-59, 6681-7107 hp, movement 0.
--   * The Highborne Summoners 11466 are creature_template faction 1355 (neutral, hostileMask 0), level 55, 522 hp, movement 0;
--     they are not trash and no plan row names them. The Residual Monstrosities 11484 are faction 834, level 59-60, 14214-14652 hp,
--     movement type 2 (waypoint): all 18 walk the same 18-point 705 yd ring (creature_movement guids 352901-352915, 341529,
--     353467-353491), each at a different phase.
--
-- CHANGES over 20261024153000 (the plan file is the source; no row is hand-set):
--   * Five crystal blocks before the Immol'thar boss step (legs 0, 2 and 4), each a pull of the crystal's four 11483 from a stand
--     15-25 yd off the pack followed by a hold on the crystal's object state (kind hold, entry the crystal, param 1 active,
--     flags 16 done-by-object, radius 40, timeout 120, entries 11483), so a remnant the pull left is fought on the spot and the step
--     ends only when the crystal reads active: steps 13 (177259), 99 (177257), 70 (leg 2, 177258), 35 (179505), 45 (179504).
--     plan-export learned Hold.object/state for this (entry the object, param the state, flag 16); the run leader already reads a
--     hold done by an object (DungeonRunPolicy.h kPlanFlagDoneObject, HoldStep). The single 11483 pulls of 20261024153000 in legs 0
--     (crystal 1: groups 6-8 and 11; crystal 2: groups 29-32; crystal 3: groups 19-21), leg 2 group 7 (crystal 3's fourth) and leg 4
--     (crystal 4: groups 17-20; crystal 5: groups 3-6) are replaced by these five blocks.
--   * The 18 Residual Monstrosity 11484 pulls are dropped (they guard nothing; the crystals are guarded by 11483 and the boss needs
--     only the crystal event). Their forced fights at the ring entrance wiped the party 5 times in r36 (steps 421 and 425: the
--     step-421 move and the first ring fight, with 11484 patrols joining), and no walkway stand is off their shared ring path. The
--     ring walk stays explicit through approach points on the three Arcane Torrent pulls and on the boss: (17 716, -128 725),
--     (-173 789, -146 885), (-86 928.5, 13.9 929.5), boss (25.07 891.66, -7.05 853.36). kill_first still names 11484 for the boss
--     fight, and no pull lists 11466.
--   * The Immol'thar boss row (leg 4 seq 74, entry 11496 at -40.45 811.14 -29.36) carries entries '' = the boss alone: the step's
--     own entry is 11496 (the plan refuses the boss in boss.first), so it waits on no Highborne Summoner. Its 300 s stall in r36
--     was Immol'thar himself, alive at the step point with UNIT_FLAG_NOT_SELECTABLE|SPAWNING: the crystal event had not completed.
--   * Path checks (server-exact, turtle-agent 940fc091 built from origin/dev f38e184 + the object-hold export): every consecutive
--     MOVE pair of the 571 rows with the pulls moving nobody: 476 of 481 pass type 0x1; the 5 that do not are the plan's older
--     long-route artifacts (leg 0 seq 3-5, seq 18-26, the duplicate seq 59/61; the leg 1-2 and leg 2 duplicate transitions), not a
--     new row. Each new stand passes from the MOVE before it: (42.67 254.13) -> (32 300) 48.3 yd; (121.07 539.2) -> (130.6 454.9)
--     87.6 yd; (-89.94 447.92) -> (-102.7 426.9) 24.6 yd; (-17.64 697.86) -> (-111.3 731.7) 101.6 yd; (51.6 855.5) -> (64 832)
--     26.6 yd; the ring chains and the stairs chain each in 50 yd hops. plan-check still lists the pre-existing leg-transition
--     server walk (the original plan's one "to" issue) and the detour/patrol notices.
-- 6 legs, 571 steps (36 + 2 + 18 + 13 + 5 + 4 pulls and 5 holds; 38 + 2 + 19 + 13 + 7 + 4 pull groups), bosses in leg order. The census fixes of round 1 and the notes of
-- round 2 are otherwise unchanged.
-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- dire_maul_west: map 429, 6 legs, 571 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_west';
-- Dungeon bosses of map 429 for this plan's boss steps only (the commander telemetry's boss rank; see 20261021114931_world.sql): the six boss
-- steps' entries, from Turtle's own world data (tortoise-wow sql/base creature_template: all six rank 1). Tsu'zee 11467 (a rank 2 rare pulled
-- explicitly) and Ferra 14308 (Illyanna's boss.first) are left out. The DELETE is scoped to these entries, not the map, so another plan's rows on
-- map 429 (the north and east wings) survive.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (429) AND `entry` IN (11489, 14690, 11488, 11487, 11496, 11486);
